      "Language": "jpn",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Recently, management of the central phlebotomy station by the clinical laboratory has become the norm and phlebotomy is a routine job for many medical technologists. Although venipuncture-related accidents, such as nerve injury, unfortunately happen in a low but fixed ratio, there is little information to avoid this risk. This topic consists of three excellent reviews: Dr. Tanabe reviewed \"Iatrogenic peripheral nerve injury; mechanism and therapy\", Dr. Ohnishi reviewed \"effective methods to prevent nerve injury at venipuncture\", and Dr. Kitamura reviewed \"An effective and efficient method of painless venipuncture in children\". I believe these three articles will be of great help to many medical technologists and clinical laboratory physicians to perform phlebotomy safely."},
